10. Definitions

"Software" means the Klavrio source code, Markdown (.md) and other project
documentation, original project assets, and accompanying materials that the
relevant copyright holder expressly distributes under this License and has
legal authority to license.

"Derivative Work" means a modification, adaptation, or other work based upon
the Software that constitutes a derivative work under applicable copyright
law.
Similarity in purpose, features, behavior, or independently developed
functionality, without copying protected expression from the Software, does
not by itself create a Derivative Work.

"Complete Corresponding Source Code" means all human-readable source code in
its preferred editable form that is reasonably necessary to understand,
modify, and reproduce the distributed executable form of the covered Software
or Derivative Work. It includes:

a. build scripts and configuration files reasonably necessary to reproduce
   the distributed executable;

b. covered project documentation reasonably necessary to understand, modify,
   and build the distributed Derivative Work; and

c. modifications and covered components incorporated into the distributed
   Derivative Work.

Complete Corresponding Source Code does not include passwords, API keys,
credentials, authentication tokens, personal or confidential information,
private AI prompts or conversations, internal development history,
tool-interaction logs, or independently licensed system libraries and tools.
These exclusions do not permit withholding any source file, build script,
configuration file, documentation, modification, or covered component that is
otherwise required by this definition. A required file containing an excluded
sensitive value must be provided with that value removed and replaced by a
documented, non-secret configuration placeholder sufficient to configure and
reproduce the build.

"Noncommercial" means use that is not intended for, directed toward, or
connected with commercial advantage, monetary compensation, business
activity, revenue generation, or any direct or indirect commercial benefit.
It excludes, without limitation:

a. selling, renting, or licensing the Software or a Derivative Work for
   payment;

b. paid hosting or managed services based on the Software or its
   functionality;

c. integration into a paid product or service;

d. internal use in a for-profit business; and

e. revenue-generating or commercially advantageous use, including use that
   provides an indirect commercial benefit.

Free personal, educational, research, and community uses are generally
permitted only when they are genuinely noncommercial under this definition.
An organization's nonprofit status does not, by itself, make a particular use
noncommercial.

